# for a server:
# /nfs/<dir-name> <host or *>(rw,sync,no_subtree_check)
#
# example:
/nfs/proxmox-nfs *(rw,sync,no_subtree_check)

# for a client (to share with macos / windows):
# /nfs/<dir-name> <host or *>(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,insecure,all_squash,anonuid=<uid>,anongid=<gid>)
#
# notes:
# make sure to create a non-root user, and uid/gid must match anon above
# macos is easy, just put the server/path in finder:
# e.g. nfs://<nfs-host>/nfs/shared-drive
#
# windows is pain, see the nfs.bat script in the windows/ dir
# For windows you also need to install NFS Client from optional features
#
# example:
/nfs/shared-drive *(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,insecure,all_squash,anonuid=1000,anongid=1000)

# Other setup information:
#
# packages which need to be installed:
# apt install nfs-kernel-server
#
# after changing the config export the filesystem again:
# exportfs -a
